2c:["$","$L3c",null,{"children":[["$","$L3d",null,{"title":"Every request fails with a permission error","id":"every-request-fails-with-a-permission-error","children":["$","p",null,{"children":"The credential chain found something, but it can't act on the bucket. Confirm\nthe service account attached to the instance or workload identity has object\nread and write on it. If it can create but not overwrite, re-uploads of a\ndigest that already exists fail, because GCS needs the delete permission to\nreplace an object."}]}],["$","$L3d",null,{"title":"The store starts but no credential was ever found","id":"the-store-starts-but-no-credential-was-ever-found","children":["$","p",null,{"children":["That's ",["$","code",null,{"children":"authentication_required"}]," at its default of ",["$","code",null,{"children":"false"}],". Set it to ",["$","code",null,{"children":"true"}],"\nso the store errors at startup instead of quietly issuing unauthenticated\nrequests."]}]}],["$","$L3d",null,{"title":"Large uploads are slow or memory-hungry","id":"large-uploads-are-slow-or-memory-hungry","children":["$","p",null,{"children":["The chunk size is at most 2 MB and each chunk is a round trip, so a large\nobject is many sequential requests; ",["$","code",null,{"children":"resumable_chunk_size"}]," can only make the\nchunks smaller. Memory per in-flight upload is bounded by the chunk size plus\nthe retry buffer; the number of concurrent requests is bounded by\n",["$","code",null,{"children":"multipart_max_concurrent_uploads"}],"."]}]}],["$","$L3d",null,{"title":"Builds are slow even though the cache is hitting","id":"builds-are-slow-even-though-the-cache-is-hitting","children":["$","p",null,{"children":["You're reaching the bucket on every read. Confirm the store is the ",["$","code",null,{"children":"slow"}]," half\nof a ",["$","code",null,{"children":"fast_slow"}]," pair, and that the ",["$","code",null,{"children":"fast"}]," half's ",["$","code",null,{"children":"eviction_policy"}]," isn't so\nsmall that everything is evicted before it's re-read."]}]}],["$","$L3d",null,{"title":"Objects exist in the bucket but Forge reports them missing","id":"objects-exist-in-the-bucket-but-forge-reports-them-missing","children":["$","p",null,{"children":["Check ",["$","code",null,{"children":"consider_expired_after_s"}],". A non-zero value makes objects older than\nthat window invisible on purpose, so they pair with a matching bucket lifecycle\nrule. If you didn't intend that, set it back to ",["$","code",null,{"children":"0"}],"."]}]}]]}]
